<p>To understand a technological object properly, we look at it with “X-ray vision”: we dissect it by applying <b>5 types of analysis</b> (the “5 magnifying glasses”). Each analysis answers a different question. As an example, we analyse a <b>backpack</b>:</p>
<div class="tbl-scroll"><table>
<tr><th>Analysis</th><th>What it studies</th><th>Key question</th><th>Example: the backpack</th></tr>
<tr><td><b>1. Anatomical</b></td><td>Shape and the parts it is made of.</td><td>What shape is it and what parts is it made of?</td><td>Straps, pockets, zips.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>2. Technical</b></td><td>Materials and tools used to make it.</td><td>What materials is it made of? What techniques were used to make it?</td><td>Nylon fabric, strong plastic.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>3. Functional</b></td><td>Usefulness and main function.</td><td>What is it for? What is its main function?</td><td>Carrying books without hurting your back.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>4. Aesthetic</b></td><td>Beauty, colour and outer finish.</td><td>What does it look like? What colours and finishes does it have?</td><td>Bright colours, sporty design.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>5. Socio-economic</b></td><td>Economic cost and impact on society and the environment.</td><td>How much does it cost and what impact does it have on society and the environment?</td><td>Affordable price, carbon footprint of its materials.</td></tr>
</table></div>
<div class="activity"><span class="tag orange">Activity</span>
  <h4>Forensic analysis (3 minutes)</h4>
  <p>Look at the object your teacher shows on the screen. Out loud, raising your hand, apply the 5 technological analyses: anatomical, technical, functional, aesthetic and socio-economic. Who dares?</p>
</div>
<div class="activity"><span class="tag orange">Activity</span>
  <h4>Quick live analysis</h4>
  <p>Choose ONE of these two objects in front of you, <b>a ballpoint pen</b> or <b>a school desk</b>, and apply the 5 magnifying glasses. Copy this table into your notebook and fill it in:</p>
  <table><tr><th style="width:30%">Analysis</th><th>My object: ____________</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Anatomical</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Technical</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Functional</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Aesthetic</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Socio-economic</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr></table>
</div>
`}},
/* 5 ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
{ id:"process", es:{ title:"El proceso tecnológico", html:()=>`
<p>Los inventores no improvisan: siguen un método ordenado, el <b>proceso tecnológico</b> (también llamado <b>método de proyectos</b>). Es como una brújula que nos guía desde el problema hasta la solución. Tiene <b>8 fases</b>:</p>
<figure class="fig">${processSVG("es")}<figcaption>La brújula del inventor: el proceso tecnológico.</figcaption></figure>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><b>Identificar el problema:</b> ¿qué necesidad tenemos?</li>
  <li><b>Buscar información:</b> investigar cómo lo han resuelto otros.</li>
  <li><b>Generar ideas:</b> tormenta de ideas (bocetos).</li>
  <li><b>Elegir la mejor solución:</b> seleccionar la más viable.</li>
  <li><b>Planificar y organizar:</b> tareas, herramientas y materiales.</li>
  <li><b>Construir el prototipo:</b> ¡manos a la obra en el taller!</li>
  <li><b>Evaluar y comprobar:</b> ¿funciona? ¿resuelve el problema?</li>
  <li><b>Presentar y comercializar:</b> elaborar la memoria y mostrarlo.</li>
</ol>
<div class="key"><b>Importante:</b> el proceso es un ciclo. Si al evaluar descubrimos que el prototipo falla, <b>volvemos atrás y rediseñamos</b>.</div>
<div class="activity"><span class="tag orange">Actividad</span>
  <h4>El circuito roto</h4>
  <p><b>Planteamiento:</b> los perros del barrio pasan mucho frío en invierno y ensucian las calles buscando refugio.</p>
  <p><b>Reto:</b> aquí tenéis 8 tarjetas de acción desordenadas. Ordenadlas del 1 al 8 siguiendo las fases del proceso tecnológico.</p>
  <div data-widget="circuit"></div>
  <details class="sol"><summary>Ver solución</summary>${circuitSolution("es")}</details>
</div>
`}, en:{ title:"The technological process", html:()=>`
<p>Inventors do not improvise: they follow an orderly method, the <b>technological process</b> (also called the <b>project method</b>). It is like a compass that guides us from the problem to the solution. It has <b>8 stages</b>:</p>
<figure class="fig">${processSVG("en")}<figcaption>The inventor’s compass: the technological process.</figcaption></figure>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><b>Identify the problem:</b> what need do we have?</li>
  <li><b>Research information:</b> find out how others have solved it.</li>
  <li><b>Generate ideas:</b> brainstorming (sketches).</li>
  <li><b>Choose the best solution:</b> select the most viable one.</li>
  <li><b>Plan and organise:</b> tasks, tools and materials.</li>
  <li><b>Build the prototype:</b> get to work in the workshop!</li>
  <li><b>Test and evaluate:</b> does it work? Does it solve the problem?</li>
  <li><b>Present and market:</b> write the report and show it.</li>
</ol>
<div class="key"><b>Important:</b> the process is a cycle. If we discover during testing that the prototype fails, <b>we go back and redesign</b>.</div>
<div class="activity"><span class="tag orange">Activity</span>
  <h4>The broken circuit</h4>
  <p><b>Situation:</b> the dogs in the neighbourhood are very cold in winter and make the streets dirty looking for shelter.</p>
  <p><b>Challenge:</b> here are 8 action cards in the wrong order. Put them in order from 1 to 8 following the stages of the technological process.</p>
  <div data-widget="circuit"></div>
  <details class="sol"><summary>Show solution</summary>${circuitSolution("en")}</details>
</div>
`}},
/* 6 ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
{ id:"team", es:{ title:"Trabajo en equipo en el taller", html:()=>`
<p>El taller no es de solitarios. Al igual que en el equipo de boxes de la Fórmula 1, <b>nadie gana solo</b>: cada miembro tiene una tarea y todos dependen de todos. En el taller trabajaréis en equipo y <b>rotaréis por 4 roles fundamentales</b>:</p>
<div class="grid2">
  <div class="box blue"><h4>Coordinador/a – Secretario/a</h4><p>Dirige al equipo, toma decisiones, completa los documentos y lleva el registro.</p></div>
  <div class="box yellow"><h4>Materiales y herramientas</h4><p>Vigila, recoge, reparte y asegura el buen estado del instrumental.</p></div>
  <div class="box red"><h4>Orden, limpieza y seguridad</h4><p>Su superpoder es la prevención: garantiza que la mesa esté despejada y que se cumplan las normas.</p></div>
  <div class="box green"><h4>Calidad y convivencia</h4><p>Fomenta el respeto, revisa que el trabajo esté bien hecho y media en los conflictos.</p></div>
</div>
`}, en:{ title:"Teamwork in the workshop", html:()=>`
<p>The workshop is not for loners. Just like a Formula 1 pit crew, <b>nobody wins alone</b>: each member has a job and everyone depends on everyone else. In the workshop you will work in teams and <b>rotate through 4 key roles</b>:</p>
<div class="grid2">
  <div class="box blue"><h4>Coordinator – Secretary</h4><p>Leads the team, makes decisions, fills in the documents and keeps the records.</p></div>
  <div class="box yellow"><h4>Materials and tools</h4><p>Watches over, collects, hands out and makes sure the tools are in good condition.</p></div>
  <div class="box red"><h4>Order, cleaning and safety</h4><p>Their superpower is prevention: they make sure the table is clear and the rules are followed.</p></div>
  <div class="box green"><h4>Quality and coexistence</h4><p>Encourages respect, checks that the work is well done and mediates in conflicts.</p></div>
</div>
`}},
